(217390, 12174, 1005, '<td valign="top">Man, can I NOT pick the winners or what!  I really liked this shot.  Nicely done and very emotional (well, it could be a personal thing with my Dad dying recently and putting him to rest at a National Cemetary, too.)</td>', 'Man, can I NOT pick the winners or what!  I really liked this shot.  Nicely done and very emotional (well, it could be a personal thing with my Dad dying recently and putting him to rest at a National Cemetary, too.)', '2003-02-17 12:39:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(217391, 12176, 5515, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the ribbon!!! Dave</td>', 'Congrats on the ribbon!!! Dave', '2003-02-17 12:39:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(217396, 12260, 5515, '<td valign="top">Thanks to all the wonderful comments on this image. I knew the "stuff" in front would be a like or don''t like thing. This is the way it was by the way, no set up involved. This is a new spur they are putting in to a factory in town and all the stuff was just laying there... Thanks again... Dave</td>', 'Thanks to all the wonderful comments on this image. I knew the "stuff" in front would be a like or don''t like thing. This is the way it was by the way, no set up involved. This is a new spur they are putting in to a factory in town and all the stuff was just laying there... Thanks again... Dave', '2003-02-17 12:41:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(217398, 12299, 4411, '<td valign="top">I didn''t vote last week so this is the first time I''ve seen this shot.<br/> <br/>What an excellent take on the challenge and a perfect title, it really does put things in perspective. The children are the perfect size - just big enough to make out, and small enough to carry the point across. Genius. And those clouds are stunning too.<br/> <br/>I''m glad to see this did so well despite not being the obvious interpretation of the challenge. Well done.</td>', 'I didn''t vote last week so this is the first time I''ve seen this shot. What an excellent take on the challenge and a perfect title, it really does put things in perspective. The children are the perfect size - just big enough to make out, and small enough to carry the point across. Genius. And those clouds are stunning too. I''m glad to see this did so well despite not being the obvious interpretation of the challenge. Well done.', '2003-02-17 12:43:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(217421, 12235, 472, '<td valign="top">thanks for your comments :)</td>', 'thanks for your comments :)', '2003-02-17 13:01:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(217439, 12220, 772, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club :)<br/> <br/>Hi Andrew...<br/> <br/>This is a great architectural shot.  I really like the patterns and designs that most architectural shots offer.  This photo also displays some very nice color in the reflection.  The bit of yellow from the steel structure on the left really pops nicely.  That special ''touch of color'' added by that element really works nicely in this photo.  I also like the diagonals created by the windows glass.  Those diagonals create your perspective for this shot quite well :)<br/> <br/>I can''t really offer you much on improvements for this shot.  <br/> <br/>Keep up the good work!<br/> <br/>John Setzler<br/> <br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club :) Hi Andrew... This is a great architectural shot.  I really like the patterns and designs that most architectural shots offer.  This photo also displays some very nice color in the reflection.  The bit of yellow from the steel structure on the left really pops nicely.  That special ''touch of color'' added by that element really works nicely in this photo.  I also like the diagonals created by the windows glass.  Those diagonals create your perspective for this shot quite well :) I can''t really offer you much on improvements for this shot.   Keep up the good work! John Setzler ', '2003-02-17 13:13:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(217463, 12280, 772, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club :)<br/> <br/>Hi Kandyj...<br/> <br/>I think you chose a good subject for an extreme angle perspective photo... I really like the contrast between the tree limbs, foliage, and the white sky.  Your desaturation idea seems to have worked very well also.  This photo has a nice chaotic feel to it... <br/> <br/>I think the only thing this photo lacks is a central point of focus for the viewer.  My eyes keep wandering around this shot and never really come to rest on some specific part of it...<br/> <br/>Excellent shot and keep up the good work :)<br/> <br/>John Setzler<br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club :) Hi Kandyj... I think you chose a good subject for an extreme angle perspective photo... I really like the contrast between the tree limbs, foliage, and the white sky.  Your desaturation idea seems to have worked very well also.  This photo has a nice chaotic feel to it...  I think the only thing this photo lacks is a central point of focus for the viewer.  My eyes keep wandering around this shot and never really come to rest on some specific part of it... Excellent shot and keep up the good work :) John Setzler', '2003-02-17 13:28:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(217550, 12174, 5212, '<td valign="top">Critique Club:<br/> <br/>Meeting the Challenge: Does this very well with the repition of the headstones.<br/> <br/>Composition:  I do think including the whole tree might have made this a bit better.  I like the tree in there, however, as it tends to add a little interest into what could have been a rather monotonous gray photo.<br/> <br/>Technical Quality:  Very well executed, the colors seem to be very right and the focus and dof good.  The lighting somehow lends a coldness to the photo, although there are shadows present so it doesn''t look flat.  The snow adds to the starkness of the cemetary as well.<br/> <br/>Creativity:  Good, wouldn''t have thought of a cemetary for rhythm.<br/> <br/>Conclusion:  A nice photo, well exectuted, might have been composed a little differently.  Good job.<br/> <br/>If you have questions or comments, don''t hesitate to write me.</td>', 'Critique Club: Meeting the Challenge: Does this very well with the repition of the headstones. Composition:  I do think including the whole tree might have made this a bit better.  I like the tree in there, however, as it tends to add a little interest into what could have been a rather monotonous gray photo. Technical Quality:  Very well executed, the colors seem to be very right and the focus and dof good.  The lighting somehow lends a coldness to the photo, although there are shadows present so it doesn''t look flat.  The snow adds to the starkness of the cemetary as well. Creativity:  Good, wouldn''t have thought of a cemetary for rhythm. Conclusion:  A nice photo, well exectuted, might have been composed a little differently.  Good job. If you have questions or comments, don''t hesitate to write me.', '2003-02-17 15:23:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(217553, 12118, 3585, '<td valign="top">Thanks to all, great start in the week! Also I am pleasently suprised to see that 4 out of the 6 ribbons this week went to black and white photos.</td>', 'Thanks to all, great start in the week! Also I am pleasently suprised to see that 4 out of the 6 ribbons this week went to black and white photos.', '2003-02-17 15:35:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(217705, 12183, 6025, '<td valign="top">(Critique Club)<br/> <br/>From the perspective, it looks as if you are standing on one of these balconies. That probably means you can support your camera on the edge of the railing. That also means you could have rested your lens on the edge, used a 1/2 second shutter time and used an ISO 200. Which would - to a very large degree - have solved the problems with this image: in all the dark areas, there is a lot of digital noise. Also, the D60 has a nasty tendency to wringing the reds up way too much.<br/> <br/>Okay, enough whining about the technical parts; Well seen, great use of your D60, and a fabulous use of the 20mm!<br/> <br/>Haje</td>', '(Critique Club) From the perspective, it looks as if you are standing on one of these balconies. That probably means you can support your camera on the edge of the railing. That also means you could have rested your lens on the edge, used a 1/2 second shutter time and used an ISO 200. Which would - to a very large degree - have solved the problems with this image: in all the dark areas, there is a lot of digital noise. Also, the D60 has a nasty tendency to wringing the reds up way too much. Okay, enough whining about the technical parts; Well seen, great use of your D60, and a fabulous use of the 20mm! Haje', '2003-02-17 18:01:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(217979, 12178, 772, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club :)<br/> <br/>Hi Doug...<br/> <br/>This photo is an excellent display of perspective... The vanishing point is clearly visible and the choice to center this composition as you have accents that nicely.  The lighting is creating an interesting mood that I can''t decide if I really like or not... Possibly if there was more light on the scene, the contrast in the foreground may be a little stronger.<br/> <br/>I think what this image may be lacking is a strong focal point.  the vanishing point of the railroad tracks seems to be the main focus of the shot.  I believe that a segment of track somewhere that had a sign or somethin that stands out in the image could create a bit stronger composition...<br/> <br/>Keep up the good work :)<br/> <br/>John Setzler<br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club :) Hi Doug... This photo is an excellent display of perspective... The vanishing point is clearly visible and the choice to center this composition as you have accents that nicely.  The lighting is creating an interesting mood that I can''t decide if I really like or not... Possibly if there was more light on the scene, the contrast in the foreground may be a little stronger. I think what this image may be lacking is a strong focal point.  the vanishing point of the railroad tracks seems to be the main focus of the shot.  I believe that a segment of track somewhere that had a sign or somethin that stands out in the image could create a bit stronger composition... Keep up the good work :) John Setzler', '2003-02-17 21:58:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(218060, 12260, 472, '<td valign="top">great work, Dave :)</td>', 'great work, Dave :)', '2003-02-17 22:21:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(218064, 12216, 472, '<td valign="top">i gave this a 9. great shot.</td>', 'i gave this a 9. great shot.', '2003-02-17 22:22:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(218388, 12176, 6627, '<td valign="top">This is great Picture I love it....!!! Great JoB</td>', 'This is great Picture I love it....!!! Great JoB', '2003-02-18 01:44:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(218411, 12306, 6172, '<td valign="top">This photo makes me want to tilt my head to adjust to the perspective of it, the photo forces me to rethink perspective.  I feel maybe it is a little too light at the top, though you might have been intending that, judging from the title.  Good focus.  I like your choice to make it a black and white.  Overall, I think you didn''t get the score you deserved, but not by much.</td>', 'This photo makes me want to tilt my head to adjust to the perspective of it, the photo forces me to rethink perspective.  I feel maybe it is a little too light at the top, though you might have been intending that, judging from the title.  Good focus.  I like your choice to make it a black and white.  Overall, I think you didn''t get the score you deserved, but not by much.', '2003-02-18 03:00:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(218426, 12201, 3540, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club<br/>By Inspzil<br/> <br/>First off, that is far and away the longest comment I''ve ever seen regarding a picture.  It will most likely be longer than my critique.<br/> <br/>Composition - I think you could''ve focused solely on the statue and gotten a good image.  The statue is my favorite part of this image.  Unfortunately I can''t stop looking at the white spot on his left foot where it looks like once there was a toe.  The spotlight on top of the wall keeps catching my attention now and again.  That would''ve been a nice thing to spot edit out as you said above.  The building looks huge, which I''m sure is what you were going for.  I like the overall composition and the choice of black and white is very good.  I think this might be a little dark for my taste though.<br/> <br/>Technical - This does look a little dark but if you lightened it up any I think you might lose the sky.  The photo looks pretty clear with good DOF.  Fill flash looks like it was a good idea, but that might be where the white spot on the toe came from.  Processing - Overall I think you did a very nice job with this one.  If there ever was a flash on the spotlight, I can''t tell.  <br/> <br/>Overall - A solid image, but a little dreary with the dark colors and greyscale.  By your description of what you did to the shot to make it better I''d say you really did a good job saving a picture.  I think the statue should''ve been a stronger part of this picture.  Hats off to your comments, they''ve proven to be helpful to some degree!!  Interesting story - Good luck in upcoming challenges - Bob</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique ClubBy Inspzil First off, that is far and away the longest comment I''ve ever seen regarding a picture.  It will most likely be longer than my critique. Composition - I think you could''ve focused solely on the statue and gotten a good image.  The statue is my favorite part of this image.  Unfortunately I can''t stop looking at the white spot on his left foot where it looks like once there was a toe.  The spotlight on top of the wall keeps catching my attention now and again.  That would''ve been a nice thing to spot edit out as you said above.  The building looks huge, which I''m sure is what you were going for.  I like the overall composition and the choice of black and white is very good.  I think this might be a little dark for my taste though. Technical - This does look a little dark but if you lightened it up any I think you might lose the sky.  The photo looks pretty clear with good DOF.  Fill flash looks like it was a good idea, but that might be where the white spot on the toe came from.  Processing - Overall I think you did a very nice job with this one.  If there ever was a flash on the spotlight, I can''t tell.   Overall - A solid image, but a little dreary with the dark colors and greyscale.  By your description of what you did to the shot to make it better I''d say you really did a good job saving a picture.  I think the statue should''ve been a stronger part of this picture.  Hats off to your comments, they''ve proven to be helpful to some degree!!  Interesting story - Good luck in upcoming challenges - Bob', '2003-02-18 05:24:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(218691, 12235, 5515, '<td valign="top">Kollin, great image. Really nice perspective... Wonderful capture... Dave</td>', 'Kollin, great image. Really nice perspective... Wonderful capture... Dave', '2003-02-18 11:48:11.000000', NULL, 0),
